fix(intel): wrap the SiP V3 command descriptor search

mailbox_get_free_cmd_desc() scans from a static free_index up to the end of
the command queue and never wraps around: it resets free_index only when it
is exactly MBOX_SVC_CMD_QUEUE_SIZE - 1 on entry. When the last two slots are
busy, the scan leaves free_index at MBOX_SVC_CMD_QUEUE_SIZE, the reset never
matches again, and every later V3 async send fails with MBOX_BUFFER_FULL
until the next reset, however empty the queue is. On a DE25-Nano (Agilex 5)
reading the SDM sensors through socfpga_hwmon while the FPGA is configured,
it hit within two minutes.

Search the whole queue circularly from the slot after the last one handed out.

--- a/plat/intel/soc/common/soc/socfpga_mailbox.c
+++ b/plat/intel/soc/common/soc/socfpga_mailbox.c
@@ -915,18 +915,16 @@
 {
 	spin_lock(&mbox_db_lock);
 	static uint32_t free_index;
+	uint32_t count, index;
 
-	/* Rollover the command queue free index */
-	if (free_index == (MBOX_SVC_CMD_QUEUE_SIZE - 1)) {
-		free_index = 0U;
-	}
-
-	for (; free_index < MBOX_SVC_CMD_QUEUE_SIZE; free_index++) {
-		if (!(mbox_svc.cmd_queue[free_index].flags &
+	for (count = 0U; count < MBOX_SVC_CMD_QUEUE_SIZE; count++) {
+		index = (free_index + count) % MBOX_SVC_CMD_QUEUE_SIZE;
+		if (!(mbox_svc.cmd_queue[index].flags &
 			MBOX_SVC_CMD_IS_USED)) {
-			mbox_svc.cmd_queue[free_index].flags |= MBOX_SVC_CMD_IS_USED;
+			mbox_svc.cmd_queue[index].flags |= MBOX_SVC_CMD_IS_USED;
+			free_index = (index + 1U) % MBOX_SVC_CMD_QUEUE_SIZE;
 			spin_unlock(&mbox_db_lock);
-			return &(mbox_svc.cmd_queue[free_index]);
+			return &(mbox_svc.cmd_queue[index]);
 		}
 	}
 
